course: dictionary
lesson: 6193
title: Strong feelings, strong words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words for unhappy are weaker than others. Sad is the everyday word. Glum is a quiet, gloomy sort of sad. Miserable is stronger: it means very unhappy. «Liam's class pretended all day that his birthday was tomorrow, and Liam was miserable, till the surprise cake.» The word shows how bad he felt before the cake.
explain: Miserable can also describe things, not just people. «So Nan's coat is still a good idea, because being freezing is miserable.» Freezing cold is unpleasant and makes you unhappy, so it is miserable. Miserable weather is grey, wet or cold weather that makes you feel low.
explain: Miserable can mean very small or poor, as in a miserable amount. The same word can also describe a grumpy person who is never cheerful, as in a miserable old man. Look at the words around it to find which meaning fits.
explain: A good check is to swap in a word you know. «He had a great many wives, and most of them quarrelled all day, which made him miserable.» Swap in very unhappy: it still makes sense, so you know you have the right meaning.
fact: Miserable means very unhappy.
fact: Miserable can describe unpleasant things, such as miserable weather.
fact: Miserable can mean very small or poor, as in a miserable amount.
fact: In British informal speech, a miserable person is grumpy and never cheerful.
fact: «Wretched» can mean miserable, as when Alice says «such a wretched height to be».
exercise: «Liam was miserable, till the surprise cake.» What does miserable mean here? | Very quiet | *Very unhappy | Happy and excited | Full of cake
exercise: «Being freezing is miserable.» What does miserable describe? | A bright, sunny day | A grumpy person | A very small amount | *Something unpleasant that makes you unhappy
exercise: Alice says «such a wretched height to be». Which word is closest in meaning to wretched? | Enormous | *Miserable | Pleasant | Glowing
test: «A miserable old man» is a British informal use. What does miserable mean here? | Lost and confused | *Grumpy and never cheerful | Very tall | Clean and tidy
test: Which word shows the strongest kind of unhappiness? | Sad | Glum | Peaceful | *Miserable
exam: «He was paid a miserable amount for all his hard work.» What does miserable mean here? | Very wet | Very large | Very happy | *Very small or poor
